<title>ESTONIA: EBRD OK'S 5 MLN DM LOAN TO TALLINNAPANK .</title>
<headline>EBRD OK'S 5 MLN DM LOAN TO TALLINNAPANK .</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) approved on Tuesday a five million mark subordinated loan to Tallinna pank, Tallinna Pank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 40 million EEK loan denominated in marks with a ten year term is to form part of the bank's capital base. </p>
<p>The principal objectives of the loan are to allow Tallinna Pank to extend its business activities, including loans to the private sector, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The agreement will be signed in London during the EBRD's general meeting to be held on April 12-15, the bank added.</p>
<p>Tallinna pank is the fourth largest bank in Estonia.</p>
<p>--David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
